Purpose: Delete the web, serve, and attach modes and the embedded web UI (Plan 0005). The opencode web, serve, and attach commands are removed. The build no longer compiles packages/app and never generates or embeds a web UI bundle, for every target including Android. The HTTP API server's catch-all UI route, the UI serving module with its embedded bundle and its app.opencode.ai proxy fallback, and the OPENCODE_DISABLE_EMBEDDED_WEB_UI runtime flag are deleted. The internal server that the TUI and run boot for themselves is not a mode and stays; only its UI route goes. Upstream tests that covered only the deleted surface are removed or trimmed inside this patch.
Upstream files: packages/opencode/script/build.ts, packages/opencode/src/cli/cmd/attach.ts, packages/opencode/src/cli/cmd/serve.ts, packages/opencode/src/cli/cmd/web.ts, packages/opencode/src/effect/runtime-flags.ts, packages/opencode/src/index.ts, packages/opencode/src/server/routes/instance/httpapi/server.ts, packages/opencode/src/server/shared/ui.ts, packages/opencode/test/cli/serve/serve-process.test.ts, packages/opencode/test/effect/runtime-flags.test.ts, packages/opencode/test/server/httpapi-ui.test.ts
Rebase note: The coupling points are the CLI entry registrations, the build script's web UI bundle step (deleted wholesale; if upstream restructures the build, keep the invariant that no web UI is compiled or embedded), and the HTTP API server's route composition, where the UI catch-all route is removed and every API route stays.

